**Discriminator**: cloud sessions have `access_token`; local sessions don't. In the renderer AuthContext I can compute `isCloudUser = !!session?.access_token`. My fetchSupabaseProfile already returns null without token (local) → profile null.

Gate design (desktop AppContent):
```tsx
const isCloudUser = !!session?.access_token;
if (!isSuperAdmin && profileLoaded && isCloudUser && !profile) → lockout ("no profile/pole")
```
But wait: what about poleless-but-profile-existing cloud user (profile exists, pole_id null)? profile exists → poleId null → has_pole_access false → writes fail; gate should ALSO block: `if (profileLoaded && isCloudUser && !isSuperAdmin && !poleId)` → lockout with message "your account is not assigned to a pole".

Local users: isCloudUser false → pass. Super admin: pass.

I need `session` in AppContent — context exposes it ✓.

Desktop AuthContext: my fetchProfile sets profileLoaded true even when the REST fetch failed transiently (null). For a cloud user whose fetch failed (network), lockout would wrongly show. Mitigate: profileLoaded = true only distinguishes... let me refine: fetchSupabaseProfile returns null for BOTH "no row" and "error". Distinguish: have it return `{ row, ok }`? Simpler: return null on no-row, THROW on network error. Then AuthContext: catch → leave profileLoaded false (retry later via db:synced listener or auth event). Let me adjust fetchSupabaseProfile: throw on !r.ok && r.status 401? For 401 (stale token) → also throw so retry happens after refresh. 404-ish other statuses → no profile → null.

